@startuml
skinparam svgDimensionStyle false
hide footbox

participant "VHL Holder" as VHLH
participant "VHL Sharer" as VHLS
participant "Trust Anchor" as TA
participant "VHL Receiver" as VHLR

== Onboarding to the trust network ==

VHLS -> TA : 01 Submit PKI Material with DID [ITI-YY1]
VHLR -> TA : 02 Submit PKI Material with DID [ITI-YY1]
VHLS -> TA : 03 Retrieve Trust List with DID [ITI-YY2]
VHLR -> TA : 04 Retrieve Trust List with DID [ITI-YY2]

== VHL issuance ==

VHLH -> VHLS : 05 Generate VHL [ITI-YY3]
VHLS --> VHLH : 06 VHL (QR code or Verifiable Credential)

== VHL presentation and document retrieval ==

VHLH -> VHLR : 07 Provide VHL [ITI-YY4]
VHLR -> VHLR : 08 Verify VHL signature\nagainst trust list
VHLR -> VHLS : 09 Retrieve Manifest [ITI-YY5]\n(ATNA secure channel)
VHLS --> VHLR : 10 Manifest\nFHIR Bundle (searchset)
VHLR -> VHLS : 11 Retrieve Document [ITI-68]
VHLS --> VHLR : 12 Documents and digital signatures

legend bottom
  Illustrative. Shows the VHL transactions applicable to the use cases
  that follow. Individual use cases exercise different subsets of this
  pattern, and the deployments described exist independently of this
  profile - they do not necessarily implement it as specified here.
endlegend

@enduml
